P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4/run-rc4-repass.sh:22,40-44` — The runner pins `a604e6b…`, while both HEAD and `origin/main` are `94a4f589…`. It therefore aborts before reviewing this candidate. Moreover, `repass-rc4/` currently contains no replacement manifest, and the tag guard exits 7 on the missing manifest. Minimal fix: pin the runner to `94a4f589…` in the pre-envelope working tree, rerun both payloads, then commit the runner, regenerated evidence, manifest, verdict fields, and signed verdict together. Any product change requires another repin and re-pass.

P2 — `.github/scripts/tests/test_validate_pair_rail_verdict.py:91-94`; `.github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:227-230` — The stricter grammar rejects the omitted legacy suite’s multiline `gpg_signature: |` fixture as an indented continuation. Consequently, even `test_canonical_envelope_is_untouched_by_the_shape_gate` fails before reaching its intended assertion. This suite is not CI-wired, so it does not invalidate the live positive controls, but it is now misleading and was excluded from the supplied payload despite being changed. Minimal fix: use the canonical single-line `base64:` signature fixture and add an explicit rejection test for block-scalar signatures; clarify the verdict template accordingly.

The production decision gates themselves are sound: canonical NO-GO, duplicate decisions, malformed fences, Unicode separators, and optional-mode attempts are blocked by the live rails, while the positive controls exercise the original authorization defect. Python 3.9 parsing, stdlib-only, contamination, counts, and diff checks were clean; full pytest execution was unavailable because the read-only reviewer sandbox provides no writable temporary directory.

