   195	  claims re-verified against behavior.
   196	
   197	### Added — spawn acceptance contract v2 (PLAN-178 Lote B, ADR-191)
   198	
   199	- **FILE ASSIGNMENT grammar with taint semantics** in
   200	  `check_agent_spawn.py`: every named spawn declares `- CAN edit:
   201	  <concrete paths>` or `- CAN edit: NONE-READ-ONLY`; globs, Unicode
   202	  whitespace, control characters or non-whitelisted list lines taint
   203	  the whole declaration. Advisory-first: omission is VISIBLE
   204	  (`spawn_file_assignment_recorded`, `path_count=0`) and the enforce
   205	  flip stays a future ceremony gated on the measure-first window.
   206	- **Fenced + capped inter-agent ingest** in the four shipped Workflow
   207	  skills (byte-identical COMMON block): PROMPT DEFENSE ≥6, explicit
   208	  FILE ASSIGNMENT, anti-spoof fencing with a 24000-char cap whose
   209	  truncation poisons the owning dimension — plus a pre-dispatch
   210	  validator of the reduced ADR-191 grammar in the workflow scripts
   211	  themselves (the Workflow rail does not pass through the spawn hook;
   212	  honest limitation recorded in ADR-191 §4).
   213	- **Shared-memory `query()` returns are fenced**
   214	  (`_lib/memory_shared.py`, ADR-089-AMEND-1) with a derivable
   215	  SEC-P0-02 reopen trigger.
   216	- **Multi-plan budget cap cure** (`check_budget.py`): the previously
   217	  INERT cap (early-allow with ≥2 active plans) now resolves the
   218	  active plan by an explicit tie-break and emits a breadcrumb instead
   219	  of silently allowing.
   220	- **Native cost cross-check in `/agent-budget`** (PLAN-178 W1.2):
   221	  a read-only, fail-soft, zero-network puller reads Claude Code's own
   222	  per-subagent usage records and `budget-summary.py` joins them
   223	  against the audit-log estimate (exact match on session + description
   224	  hash, ordinal fallback; unmatched residue VISIBLE on both sides;
   225	  cache-billable split priced correctly). Opt-in via `--native` /
   226	  `CEO_BUDGET_NATIVE=1` — the default output stays byte-identical —
   227	  with a `CEO_NATIVE_COST_DISABLE` kill-switch. Doctrine recorded in
   228	  the command doc: a cross-check, never an authority swap.
   229	- **Vacuous-check lint + a live cure** (PLAN-178 Lote A):
   230	  `check-vacuous-checks.py` fails any boot check whose reachable local
